; Validate the grammar spec artifact. This does NOT build a parser: nothing
; consumes one, and --no-code-generation means none is produced. What the rule
; buys is the check -- menhir builds the LR automaton, and --strict turns every
; shift/reduce and reduce/reduce conflict into an error, so an ambiguity in the
; grammar fails the test suite instead of sitting unnoticed in a document.
;
; menhir is invoked as an ordinary program rather than through dune's (menhir)
; stanza. That keeps dune-project free of a (using menhir ...) line and means
; nothing else in this build acquires a menhir dependency: it is a build-time
; dependency of this one artifact, never a runtime dependency of the
; interpreter, the CLI or the VSCode extension.
;
; To see WHY a conflict happened, add --explain and read n88basic.conflicts:
;   menhir --explain --strict --unused-tokens --no-code-generation \
;     spec/grammar/n88basic.mly
(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (run menhir --strict --unused-tokens --no-code-generation %{dep:n88basic.mly})))
